  "settle_ms": 200,
  "note": "Two sessions persisted with the first active; the leader+l chord opens the session-list dialog over the session surface, both stub sessions listed. Both sides must render the same dialog overlay (two rows, cursor on the first) plus the underlying transcript. GAP (explicitly out of scope this round): driving the dialog further (down+enter, opening the second session and exposing the tab rail) never reaches a resting frame on the rust side (no settle within 64 pumps), so the tab-rail switch path is deferred to T9/T10 as a recorded finding; the ref fixture itself cannot assemble a multi-tab boot because the driver boots a single active session."
